      <Single Name="Object" Type="{ffbfa93a-b94d-45fc-a329-229860183b1d}" Method="IArchivable">
        <Single Name="Interface" Type="{a9ed5b7e-75c5-4651-af16-d2c27e98cb94}" Method="IArchivable">
          <Single Name="TextDocument" Type="{f3878285-8e4f-490b-bb1b-9acbb7eb04db}" Method="IArchivable">
            <Single Name="TextBlobForSerialisation" Type="string">(*
	GVL_TeltonikaCredentials                                  Revised 22.08.2026
	==========================================================================
	WHAT THIS LIST IS FOR
	The single place where the Teltonika router login is maintained. Both the
	older prg_SendSMS and the newer prg_AlarmSMS read from here, so a
	changed password only has to be entered once.

	WHY THE CREDENTIALS ARE RETAIN AND THE REST IS NOT
	Teltonika_Username and Teltonika_Password are VAR_GLOBAL RETAIN, so they
	keep their value through a PLC restart and can be corrected online without
	rebuilding and downloading. That matters because a password change on the
	router would otherwise take a full engineering session to follow.
	The remaining entries are ordinary globals: they belong to the project and
	should come back from the source on every download.

	WHY THE PASSWORD IS BLANK IN THE SOURCE
	So the secret is not stored in the project file, which gets copied, backed
	up and shared. Enter it ONCE online and the retain keeps it.
	If you do decide to put it in the source anyway, remember that the dollar
	sign is the escape character in ST and must be doubled. Ordinary characters
	such as the at sign need no escaping.

	VERIFIED 22.08.2026 ON rutx09-hyc
	The whole API flow - login, modem status returning id 3-1, and send - works
	with the ADMIN user. A separate low privilege user named pfc300 was refused
	with HTTP 401 code 120: it either does not exist on that router, or its user
	group has no API access. To move to a dedicated API user later, create it on
	the correct router, put it in a group allowed to reach the messages
	endpoints, and change the two retain values online. No code change needed.

	Do not publish or share this file.
*)
{attribute 'qualified_only'}
VAR_GLOBAL
	// prg_AlarmSMS therefore overrides the host locally in its own
	// sRouterOverride, and only borrows the credentials from here.
	// Written WITHOUT the https prefix - the send block adds that itself.
	Teltonika_sRouterIP	: STRING := 'rutx09.tailescale.ts.net';

	// Default recipient and message for the older prg_SendSMS. The alarm
	// system does not use these; it keeps its own recipient list.
	Teltonika_Number	: STRING[64] := '+4791919191';
	Teltonika_sMessage	: STRING := 'Debug test SMSCodesys';
END_VAR

VAR_GLOBAL RETAIN
	// Router API user. Must have API rights - an ordinary low privilege user
	// is refused with 401 code 120 even when the password is correct.
	Teltonika_Username	: STRING[64] := 'admin';

	// Blank on purpose, see the note in the header. Enter it online once.
	Teltonika_Password	: STRING[64] := '';
END_VAR</Single>
